Design: We integrate Mixup data augmentation into the training loop by randomly mixing pairs of images, labels, and corresponding sample weights with a Beta(α=0.2) distribution. This encourages the model to learn more robust and fair representations by handling convex combinations of samples. We keep the weighted BCE loss, OneCycleLR scheduler, partial freezing of DenseNet121, and TenCrop TTA inference unchanged. We then perform 5-fold cross-validation with Mixup and print the updated mean CV AUROC.
