Design: I propose enhancing the training data augmentation pipeline by replacing the simple Resize+CenterCrop with stronger, more diverse transforms: RandomResizedCrop, random horizontal and vertical flips, small rotations, color jitter, and RandomErasing applied before normalization. This atomic change will improve the model’s robustness and generalization across different skin tones without altering the core training loop, loss, or inference TTA. We keep the existing Mixup, OneCycleLR scheduler, weighted BCE loss, partial freezing of DenseNet121, and TenCrop TTA unchanged. We then rerun 5‐fold cross‐validation to measure the impact on mean AUROC.
